What does this program print?

```swift
protocol Greeter { func hello() -> String }
extension Greeter {
    func hello() -> String { "hello" }
    func wave() -> String { "wave" }
}
struct Polite: Greeter {
    func hello() -> String { "good day" }
    func wave() -> String { "bow" }
}
let g: any Greeter = Polite()
print(g.hello(), g.wave(), Polite().wave())
```

What does this program print?

```swift
func pairUp<T>(_ a: [T], _ b: [T]) -> [[T]] {
    zip(a, b).map { [$0, $1] }
}
print(pairUp([1, 2, 3], [4, 5]))
```

